hey it's david2 and welcome back to  what's new in networking where we cover  well what's new in networking today i'll  provide some new updates for the network  intelligence center so let's dive right  in  [Music]  networks are at the foundation of an  environment you need a pane of glass  that can provide a multitude of tools to  troubleshoot diagnose and monitor your  environment  network intelligence center provides  that single console for managing google  cloud network visibility monitoring  verification and optimization today  there are currently four modules in the  network intelligence center network  topology connectivity tests performance  dashboard and firewall insights today  we'll be covering new enhancements for  the connectivity test and the  performance dashboard diving right in  connectivity test is a configuration and  route analyzer that lets you diagnose  connectivity issues in your vpc network  due to a misconfiguration or due to  missing routes when analyzing network  configurations connectivity test uses an  abstract state machine to model how a  vpc network should process packets  google cloud processes the packet in  several logical steps  previously connectivity test was purely  a configuration analyzer with the launch  of dynamic reachability verification we  introduced live data plane analysis  dynamic verification tests connectivity  by sending multiple trace packets from  the source endpoint to the destination  the dynamic verification results show  you the number of probes  the number of probes that successfully  reach the destination and a reachability  status the status is determined based on  how many probes were successfully  delivered reachability is more than 95  percent unreachable is zero percent and  partial reachable is between zero and  ninety five percent  in addition to showing how many packets  were successfully delivered dynamic  verification also shows median and 95th  percentile one-way latency information  the last topic today will be the  performance dashboard performance  dashboard gives you the visibility into  the performance of your project's  resources as well as the performance of  the entire google cloud network  it will provide you with packet loss and  latency details so how does it work  performance dashboard runs workers on  physical hosts that house your vms  these workers insert and receive pro  packets that run on the same network as  your traffic because the workers run on  the physical host and not on the vms  these workers do not consume vm  resources and the traffic is not visible  to your vms  what about latency for latency  latency is measured by tcp packets based  on the sample of your actual traffic  latency is calculated as the time that  elapsed between sending the tcp sequence  number and receiving the corresponding  act that contains network rtt and tcp  stack related delay the ui shows latency  as the median of all the relevant  measurements  in the project performance view  performance dashboard shows packet loss  and latency for zones where you have  compute engine resources for your  project this release introduces a  performance dashboard for all of google  cloud the dashboard presents the overall  google cloud metrics for each possible  google cloud zone pair  it displays the current status of google  cloud network and lets you compare  performance across all of google cloud  to the performance observed in your  projects  similar to project view performance will  be shown via summary charts and heat  maps for both packet loss and latency  and you have the ability to review six  weeks of history so that's all we have  for this episode of what's new in  networking check out the links below to  learn more about network intelligence  center and stay tuned for the next  episode of what's new in networking  you
 

